

🧠 Hypothetical Example

Input (English): "The cat eats"
Output (French): "Le chat mange"

⸻

🧾 Vocabulary and Embedding Setup

Input (English) tokens:

Word	Index	Embedding
The	1	[0.1, 0.3]
Cat	2	[0.2, 0.4]
Eats	3	[0.6, 0.9]

X = [x₁, x₂, x₃] = [[0.1, 0.3], [0.2, 0.4], [0.6, 0.9]]  # shape: (3, 2)

Output (French) tokens:

Word	Index	Embedding
	0	[0.0, 0.0]
Le	1	[0.3, 0.4]
Chat	2	[0.2, 0.5]
Mange	3	[0.6, 0.1]


⸻

✅ Step-by-Step Vectorized Implementation

⸻

🟢 1. Encoder (Bi)LSTM – forward only here for clarity

Assume:
	•	Hidden size: 1 (scalar)
	•	Weights:
W_x^{enc} = [0.5, 0.1], W_h^{enc} = 0.3

⸻

Forward Pass:

h_1 = \tanh(0.5·0.1 + 0.1·0.3 + 0) = \tanh(0.08) ≈ 0.08
h_2 = \tanh(0.5·0.2 + 0.1·0.4 + 0.3·0.08) = \tanh(0.164) ≈ 0.162
h_3 = \tanh(0.5·0.6 + 0.1·0.9 + 0.3·0.162) = \tanh(0.4386) ≈ 0.412

H = [h₁, h₂, h₃] = [0.08, 0.162, 0.412]


⸻

🔵 2. Decoder Initialization
	•	Initial state: s₀ = h₃ = 0.412
	•	Decoder input at t=1: <START> → [0.0, 0.0]
	•	Decoder weights:
W_x^{dec} = [0.6, 0.2], W_h^{dec} = 0.3

⸻

🟠 3. Decoder Step at t = 1

(a) Compute decoder hidden state s_1:

s_1 = \tanh(W_x·y₀ + W_h·s₀)
= \tanh(0 + 0.3·0.412) = \tanh(0.1236) ≈ 0.123

⸻

(b) Compute alignment scores (dot product):

e_{1j} = s_1 × h_j
\Rightarrow [0.123·0.08, 0.123·0.162, 0.123·0.412]
= [0.0098, 0.0199, 0.0507]

⸻

(c) Softmax attention weights:

\alpha_{1j} = \text{softmax}(e_{1j}) = [0.327, 0.331, 0.341]

⸻

(d) Compute context vector:

c_1 = \sum_j \alpha_{1j}·h_j = 0.327·0.08 + 0.331·0.162 + 0.341·0.412
= 0.2204

⸻

(e) Combine & Predict output:

Let:

W_pred = [0.7, 0.3]
z = 0.7·c₁ + 0.3·s₁ = 0.7·0.2204 + 0.3·0.123 = 0.1909

Vocabulary projection:

W_vocab = [0.1, 0.3, 0.6]  # ["<START>", "Le", "chat"]
scores = W_vocab × z = [0.0191, 0.0573, 0.1145] → softmax → max at index 2 → "chat"

✅ Predicted: "chat" (we expected "Le"; the architecture is correct, weights need learning)

⸻

🔁 Repeat for t = 2 and t = 3:

Now, decoder input becomes:
	•	t=2 → "chat" → [0.2, 0.5]
	•	t=3 → "mange" → [0.6, 0.1]
And same steps are repeated:
New s₂, new alignment scores e₂j, new attention weights α₂j, new context c₂, then z₂, then predicted y₂.

